expression: "render_warnings(\"let unused = \\\"x\\\"\\nfind 0+ any \\\"x\\\" or \\\"<\\\" until \\\">\\\" or newline\")"
---
  ⚠ `until` applies only to `">"` here, not to the whole `or`
   ╭─[pattern:2:24]
 1 │ let unused = "x"
 2 │ find 0+ any "x" or "<" until ">" or newline
   ·                        ─────────
   ╰────
  help: to stop at any of the options, write `until (">" or newline)`
  ⚠ `0+ any` takes everything, so `"x"` can never match after it
   ╭─[pattern:2:13]
 1 │ let unused = "x"
 2 │ find 0+ any "x" or "<" until ">" or newline
   ·             ───
   ╰────
  help: use `until "x"` to match up to it
  ⚠ rule `unused` is never used
